  "findings": [
    "Stock Ghidra shows that the private workqueue allocation precedes ram_work_init. The initial delayed work is queued on system_wq with delay 2000 jiffies; at the pinned HZ=250 configuration this is 8 seconds.",
    "Stock probe calls ram_work_init before allocating the RTP buffer at +0x608 and FIFO pages at +0x610. The later allocation-failure paths release the IRQ and return zero without publishing g_aw_haptic, leaving the wrapper to detect and clean the partial state.",
    "Before this change, ram_work_routine could reach RAM state mutation and request_firmware_nowait before the wrapper marked probe_complete. The current source gates both effects on haptic_lifetime_is_probe_complete and requeues the delayed work after 250 jiffies while probe remains incomplete.",
    "The retry path checks shutdown before it requeues. The pinned target cancel_delayed_work_sync implementation disables the work while flushing and guarantees no pending or executing instance on return unless another enqueue races; the shutdown gate prevents continued retry after removal begins.",
    "When the private workqueue is NULL, stock probe did not call ram_work_init, so no +0x3c0 work exists. After ram_work_init has run, the queue pointer is non-NULL and aw_remove performs cancel, callback-count drain, and a second cancel before destroying the queue or retiring state.",
    "The asynchronous firmware callback remains counted through ram_load. A failed ram_load can enqueue a retry on system_wq before decrementing that count; the second remove-time cancel catches that retry after the callback drain. ram_update_store is exposed only after probe setup and is drained by LED/sysfs unregister before teardown continues."
  ],
  "conclusion": "The pre-publication initial RAM-worker window is statically gated in candidate 53ee12ee85c0d39eb05515e81b7eff5abe14af4480a4b7376ddbebc902427bb3. The existing asynchronous callback drain and double delayed-work cancellation still cover submitted firmware callbacks and system_wq retries. This is not runtime, fault-injection, or hardware validation.",
  "remaining_status": "The whole-driver reconstruction and canonical ABI/import audit remain INCOMPLETE; this focused review does not promote a function to exact stock equivalence."
}
